From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herlon Aguiar <3419441+mxfp0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Port the native SM12x TileLang backend to vLLM 0.32

Upstream base: vllm-project/vllm v0.32.0, 5df63a7203cdb9328d824a27b682e77c7b9928be.
Rationale: retain the r6x native DeepSeek V4.1 kernel family, compact MXFP4
KV/indexer storage, Engram disk reader, exact routed scale codes and DSpark
verification while adopting the official model registry and V2 runner APIs.
Use B12X 1.5.1 direct checkpoint I/O through a bounded native loader; filter
Engram table tensors by checkpoint metadata and preserve original file offsets.
Keep model preparation before distributed warm-up, bound speculative padding,
and avoid full-vocabulary work on the native greedy verification path.

Quality: preserve native checkpoint precision, FP32 logits, WO-A activation
quantization and reference SwiGLU/NaN behavior. Optimized greedy verification
is limited to eligible requests; ordinary sampling keeps the upstream path.
The optional SPARK3_GREEDY_MIN_TOKENS mask preserves stop-token constraints.
No checkpoint rewrite, site-local Engram mapping or external NCCL is required.

Tests: checkpoint routing and mixed-shard filtering, native configuration and
stock file offsets, greedy verification, DFlash preparation, dead rows,
rejection chunking, TileLang attention, MoE and vocabulary numerical tests.
Upstream status: local candidate port; not submitted to vllm-project/vllm.
The native family is carried from spark-ds41f r6x, not newly introduced here.

